r GI Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Faculty & Staff Breadcrumb Home Faculty & Staff Career Champions The Center for Career and Leadership Development is excited to announce our new Career Champions Program! Career Champions is a campus wide program designed to visibly identify faculty and staff who are especially equipped to assist students with career decision making. Classroom Presentations When faculty and staff partner with the Center for Career and Leadership Development, together we can make a powerful difference in the long-term, professional success of our students. On-Campus Student Employment Need a student to work for you on a part-time, research, or temporary assignment on campus. Letters of Reference You often observe things like a student's punctuality, ability to work with others and how they confront challenges. In a strong field of candidates, these insights may provide an employer with important information that a GPA and resume can't always reflect. For students with little or no professional experience, professors and co-op or internship supervisors become likely candidates to write letters of reference on the student's behalf. Employer Referrals Do employers call your department to ask for student referrals? Quinncia Quinncia is an interactive artificial intelligence-based platform which helps students to build a strong resume and to excel at interviewing. If you are interested using Quinncia in class, please email Jenna Rowlands at jmrowlan@odu.edu for more information. Impact Learning Communities Learning Communities are groups of students who connect what they are learning with what they want to do: their majors, career choices, and/or their hopes for a better world. Learning Community students take one or more courses together and are open to students living on- or off- campus. Service Learning Service-learning is a type of experiential learning which integrates community-based experiences and projects into a course's curriculum, and allows students to apply their classroom knowledge while addressing real world community issues. Career Treks Consider bringing your students to an employer to gain a better understanding of various professions and job culture. An ideal visit includes a tour of the work site/facility, a briefing about the company, and a discussion panel of employees. Many employers are happy to give back and promote their brand to prospective employees. The Center for Career and Leadership Development can assist with connecting with an employer host, establishing a schedule for the Trek, and transportation arrangements and costs. Contact the Experiential Learning Team at experientiallearning@odu.edu to enhance your classroom experience! Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube CCLD Spring 2026 Newsletter Attend the ODU Career Summit This conference connects recruiters with ODU faculty and staff, featuring sessions on building talent pipelines and supporting students in their career goals. Learn more about the summit 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
