gures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Navigation Back Academics Academic Programs Back Academic Programs All Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs ODUGlobal Continued Learning Colleges & Schools Back Colleges & Schools All Colleges & Schools Batten College of Engineering & Technology Brock Virginia Health Sciences Brock Virginia Health Sciences Eastern Virginia Medical School Ellmer College of Health Sciences Ellmer School of Nursing EVMS School of Health Professions Joint School of Public Health Darden College of Education & Professional Studies Perry Honors College Strome College of Business College of Arts and Letters College of Sciences Graduate School School of Cybersecurity School of Data Science School of Supply Chain, Logistics & Maritime Operations Academic Resources Back Academic Resources Academic Calendar Academic Success Educational Accessibility University Catalogs University Libraries You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Admission Future Students Back Future Students Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Medical Students International Admissions ODUGlobal Military & Veterans Admitted Students Back Admitted Students Undergraduate Graduate International Returning Students Cost & Aid Back Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships Cost Estimator GI Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Alumni Opportunities Breadcrumb Home Alumni Opportunities At CCLD, we’re here to support you—whether you’re a recent graduate taking your first steps into the professional world or a seasoned professional exploring new career opportunities. Our dedicated team provides personalized guidance tailored to your career and leadership goals, ensuring that you have the resources and support you need at every stage of your journey. Our Services for Alumni Include: Virtual Career Coaching Corner: Join our monthly virtual workshops on emerging career topics such as job search strategies, professional development, and industry trends. These sessions are open to all ODU alumni and accessible through Handshake. View the full schedule and upcoming sessions here . Personalized Career Coaching: Receive expert advice and personalized career support from one of our experienced career coaches. Schedule a one-on-one consultation through Handshake using the Career Center tab to get started. Virtual appointments are available via Handshake for your convenience. Job Search Assistance: Explore our comprehensive job database on HANDSHAKE , where you can search and apply for hundreds of entry-level, mid-career, and professional roles across industries. Career Resources Hub: Access a wide range of tools to enhance your job search, including resume guides, interview tips, networking strategies, and more. Whether you’re preparing for a career change or moving up in your field, our resources will help you stand out. Career Fairs and Networking Events: Attend our virtual and in-person career fairs to connect with employers and expand your network. Take the next step in your career journey with confidence—schedule your career coaching session today and unlock the full potential of our career services. Get Set for Success Resumes Job Search & Networking Strategies Interviewing & Evaluating an Offer Using Handshake After Graduation As you transition from student to alumni, you will continue to have access to Handshake for job searches, employer messaging, and career resources. To ensure uninterrupted access after your ODU email deactivates, please complete the steps below. Access link: https://odu.joinhandshake.com/edu 1. Log in Through the ODU Handshake Portal Visit https://odu.joinhandshake.com/edu . Select Students & Alumni and choose Old Dominion University . Sign in using your ODU email. If you are redirected to ODU Single Sign-On (SSO), continue to Step 2. 2. Create Handshake Login Credentials (If You Previously Used SSO) Handshake requires personal login once your ODU SSO access ends. On the SSO screen, select “Or log in using your Handshake credentials.” Click Get Started . Check your inbox and open the Set My Password email. Create a password following the instructions provided. 3. Add a Personal Email to Your Account Click your profile icon → Settings . Under Emails , select + Add another email . Enter your personal email and confirm it using the link sent to your inbox.  (see below) 4. Set Your Personal Email as Your Primary Email Return to Settings → Emails . Select the three dots next to your personal email. Choose Make Primary . 5. Update Your Profile to Reflect Alumni Status Navigate to your Profile . Update your Education section with your graduation month/year. Ensure your status reflects completion of your degree. Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
    },
