ll Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit About Us Breadcrumb Home About Us Mission Statement The mission of the Center for Career & Leadership Development is to empower students and alumni from their first day as Monarchs through graduation and their careers by providing innovative programs, comprehensive resources, personalized guidance, and intentional engagement with community partners to foster the development of essential career skills and leadership qualities. We inspire lifelong learning, facilitate important connections for career readiness, and support the critical needs of our community, ensuring they are well-prepared to navigate and excel in a dynamic global landscape. Vision Statement The Center for Career & Leadership Development, in collaboration with campus and community partners, will support ODU students and alumni in their career and leadership exploration, learning, development, and achievement. Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube Our Values Empowerment: To inspire and enable a journey of self-exploration, confidence, and continuous learning Intentional Inclusion: A holistic approach to providing culturally aware and equitable access, engagement, representation, and outreach Strategic Collaboration: The development of meaningful and intentional relationships to achieve mutually beneficial goals and outcomes Student Success: Outcomes that encompass ongoing professional readiness, developing a sense of security and belonging, and promoting intentional academic achievement and community engagement Our Goals Support students as they explore careers and connect to resources that aid in career and leadership development. Facilitate opportunities for students to strengthen and articulate their NACE career readiness competencies and leadership qualities. Provide structured support to students and alumni as they navigate transitions and promote retention and success. Provide resources, opportunities, and support for internal and external partners to promote students’ career and leadership development. Equip CCLD professional, graduate student, and undergraduate student staff to develop and enhance themselves and contribute to a positive work environment. 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
