editation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Navigation Back Academics Academic Programs Back Academic Programs All Programs Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs ODUGlobal Continued Learning Colleges & Schools Back Colleges & Schools All Colleges & Schools Batten College of Engineering & Technology Brock Virginia Health Sciences Brock Virginia Health Sciences Eastern Virginia Medical School Ellmer College of Health Sciences Ellmer School of Nursing EVMS School of Health Professions Joint School of Public Health Darden College of Education & Professional Studies Perry Honors College Strome College of Business College of Arts and Letters College of Sciences Graduate School School of Cybersecurity School of Data Science School of Supply Chain, Logistics & Maritime Operations Academic Resources Back Academic Resources Academic Calendar Academic Success Educational Accessibility University Catalogs University Libraries You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Admission Future Students Back Future Students Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Medical Students International Admissions ODUGlobal Military & Veterans Admitted Students Back Admitted Students Undergraduate Graduate International Returning Students Cost & Aid Back Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships Cost Estimator GI Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Student Employment & Other Opportunities Breadcrumb Home Student Employment & Other Opportunities Seeking Student Employment? Your first stop is Handshake! Connect to open positions and many types of opportunities, both on- and off-campus in Handshake. Explore Opportunities Federal Work Study (FWS) Provides funds for part-time employment to help eligible students finance the costs of postsecondary education. All available FWS positions are posted in Handshake. FWS funds are not applied to your student account. Funds must be earned through employment in an eligible FWS position within the university and are paid through direct deposit based on hours worked. A current FWS Award offer is required to apply for all FWS positions. An award does not guarantee a position on campus, but instead opens an additional pool of positions available to you on campus. The Center for Career and Leadership Development partners with all campus departments for FWS allocations. Each position is posted in Handshake and applicants are recruited and hired directly by the worksite. To find available positions, please log into Handshake and search for “FWS” positions. Federal Work Study Off-Campus FWS Internship Program Eligibility Check your award notification from Financial Aid or LEO Online . Eligible students who filed a FAFSA form for financial aid are given FWS amount to accept or decline from the Old Dominion University Office of Financial Aid. FWS is awarded by Financial Aid based on financial need as determined through your completed FAFSA. Eligibility is determined by number of factors. If you are awarded FWS you will see the award in your Financial Aid Package. Check your financial aid package in LEO Online. FWS will be listed with any other grants or loans issued by Financial Aid. Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube Learn & Earn Program (LEAP) LEAP is a freshman employment program unique to ODU that allows students to mix Learning with Earning. ONLY freshman with a LEAP award are able to apply for open LEAP jobs. Students in this program are hired in different departments around campus and are able to earn a paycheck while also taking a weekly class that will teach about professionalism and other workforce readiness skills. LEAP seeks to prepare students for the internships and careers after college. Learning about the skills employers value while developing and applying them to their work site is the basis of the program. The LEAP program is only for freshmen. There is a LEAP2 program that allows some of the successful LEAP1 students to continue into their sophomore year. The LEAP Program continues from LEAP 1 to LEAP 4 allows students to work on campus in a role that will help to develop career-relevant skills while preparing students for internships or other work options until graduation. Students have to have completed LEAP 1 and continue to be eligible for the program to participate. LEAP STAT Eligibility Check your award notification from Financial Aid. Eligible 1st year undergraduate students who filed a FAFSA form for financial aid would have been given an LEAP amount to accept or decline from the Old Dominion University Office of Financial Aid. LEAP is awarded by Financial Aid based on financial need as determined through your completed FAFSA. Eligibility is determined by number of factors. If you are awarded LEAP you will see the award in your Financial Aid Package. Check your financial aid package in LEO. LEAP will be listed with any other grants or loans issued by Financial Aid. To accept your award go to the LEO Online Financial Aid review screen, choose accept (or decline) the LEAP offer. Once accepted, LEAP awards must be earned by attending the LEAP class and obtaining a LEAP position on campus; LEAP awards are not automatically applied to your student account. Apply for Jobs on Handshake Once you have accepted a FWS or LEAP award you can search for a position that will allow you to earn your award: Log into Handshake Upload your resume Click “Jobs” Filter by “On Campus Student Employment” Search “FWS” or “LEAP” All available positions are posted and new positions are added regularly. If you do not find a suitable position, please save a job Search Agent to receive an automated job update: Select the \"Advanced Search\" tab to save, name, and submit your search Schedule your search from the \"Search Agent's\" tab Application to Work Study Jobs is a similar process to application to any other position. Make sure that your resume speaks to your skills. If you need any assistance, please visit the Career Commons to discuss your resume. A FWS or LEAP award does not guarantee employment. Like any other job, FWS and LEAP have a competitive hiring process and you will need to complete a job search in Handshake. There are a limited amount of opportunities each semester, so apply early. Internships & Cooperative Education (Co-Ops) The Monarch Internship & Co-Op Office serves as the central unit for supporting work-based learning initiatives at Old Dominion University. They provide advising and support to students, collaborate with employers, and work with academic departments to expand work-based learning curricula. For more information, please contact the Monarch Internship and Co-Op Office at 757-683-5627, internship@odu.edu , odu.edu/internship , or visit the office at 1000 Webb Center, Monday - Friday, 8:30 am to 5:00 pm. 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
    },
