rships Cost Estimator GI Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Living-Learning & Theme Communities Breadcrumb Home Living-Learning & Theme Communities Image Living-Learning Communities Living-Learning Communities (LLCs) provide students the opportunity to live and engage with other students who have similar academic, professional, and/or co-curricular interests. LLCs require enrollment in specific courses. Learn more about the application process Theme Communities Theme Communities (TCs) are designed to provide students with an opportunity to engage with other students in a residential community surrounding a particular theme or topic area of interest. These communities are provided with educational and social events to further explore that topic of interest. Why should I participate? Benefits of participating in a Living-Learning or Theme Community: Connecting with peers that share similar academic interests and career pursuits Access to in-hall academic peer mentors, tutoring, study groups or tables, etc. More interaction with college faculty and networking opportunities Experiencing a smoother transition to college Participating in events/activities outside of the classroom Peer Mentors (PMs) with academic interest or personal passions that are similar students in the LLC Looking for more ways to get connected and engaged? See more here. Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Living-Learning Communities 757-683-5881 LLC Office livinglearning@odu.edu 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 Interested in a Learning Community? We can connect you with the right people! Interest Form Apply to be a Peer Mentor Peer Mentors provide student leadership for these communities. Apply Now Impact Learning Communities ILC students take one or more courses together and live on- or off- campus. Learn more First-Year Communities Living-Learning & Theme communities that first-year students entering Old Dominion University can apply to join through their housing application. First-Year Communities Transfer & Upperclass Communities Living-Learning & Theme communities that transfer and upperclass students can apply to join through their housing application. Transfer & Upperclass Communities How to Apply Learn more about the application process 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
