I Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Career Fairs Breadcrumb Home Career Fairs The Center for Career & Leadership Development sponsors various career fairs throughout the academic year. Active participation in our career fairs gives employers an opportunity to market and talk to students, alumni, and local military personnel about their organization. Fall Fairs Business Fair Career & Internship Fair Health & Human Services Fair Student Job and Volunteer Fair Spring Fairs Business Fair Career & Internship Fair Health & Human Services Fair Student Job and Volunteer Fair Upcoming Events Register Oct 14 Graduate & Alumni Career Coaching Corners - The Ultimate Guide to Tech Jobs 12 pm Oct 20 Fall 2026 Resume Refresh: Get Ready for the Career Fair! 9 am Dec 8 Senior Send Off 11 am Payment The Center for Career and Leadership Development sets payment deadlines for each event. These are identified within the event itself. All payment must be received prior to the event itself. The Center for Career and Leadership Development reserves the right to restrict access to recruiting activities for failure to pay an outstanding invoice. Cancellation Policy The Center for Career & Leadership Development sets cancellation deadlines for each career fair/event which are typically 2 to 3 weeks before the event date.  These are identified on the Handshake registration page for each individual event.  All cancellations must be submitted in writing via email to employers@odu.edu .  No cancellations will be accepted over the phone or in-person.  Organizations cancelling before the cancellation deadline will receive a refund minus the $50 non-refundable processing fee.  If your organization encounters an extenuating circumstance, please contact the Employer Relations team for additional information. Rain or Shine Policy The Center for Career & Leadership Development hosts several career fairs throughout the year and all events will occur rain or shine.  In the event a career fair has to be cancelled or rescheduled due to extreme weather or a University mandated closure, any amount already paid by the organization will be applied to the rescheduled date or a career fair of the equivalent size and scope occurring in the next semester (or year if the event is only held once per academic year).  If you would like to request a refund, please submit your request in writing via email to employers@odu.edu . No Show Policy Organizations that do not check in by the start of the career fair on the day of the event will be considered a “no show.”   The Center for Career & Leadership Development reserves the right to restrict access to recruiting activities due to perpetual no shows. Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
