tor GI Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Employer Partners Breadcrumb Home Employer Resources Employer Partners Partner With Us The Center for Career and Leadership Development Employer Partner Program offers an opportunity for employers to demonstrate their commitment and financial support to Old Dominion University. Partner with us to support career education while enhancing your recruitment efforts of Monarchs. For inquiries about supporting the Center for Career and Leadership Development at any partner level, please contact the Employer Relations Team at employers@odu.edu . Diamond $20,000 Two booth registrations, admission for four representatives, and an electrical connection at the in-person Fall and Spring Career & Internship Fairs. Premier booth placement at the Career & Internship Fair (based on consultation with Center for Career and Leadership Development staff). Prominent recognition of partnership at the Fall and/or Spring Career & Internship Fair (based on semester(s) selected) through on-site print and digital signage. Prominent recognition of partnership on the Center for Career and Leadership Development website, within the office, on a display outside of the suite, and on the Guidebook app used for the Career & Internship Fairs. Career opportunities social media campaign on Instagram to include four graphics and three videos. Two email campaigns (once each semester) to highlight career opportunities to targeted population. Access to resume book (once each semester) of targeted population distributed to designated employer representative. Employer registration for four representatives to annual ODU Career Summit. Custom introduction and communication to relevant student organizations (up to five). Hosted lunch and learn session with relevant student leaders and campus partners/faculty. A customized industry day on campus for students and campus partners/faculty. Guaranteed interview room space (up to six rooms) in the Center for Career and Leadership Development suite in the days after the Fall and Spring Career & Internship Fair (based on semester(s) selected). Presenting partner for the CCLD Career Champions Program. Platinum $15,000 Two booth registrations, admission for four representatives, and an electrical connection at the in-person Fall and Spring Career & Internship Fairs. Premier booth placement at the Career & Internship Fair (based on consultation with Center for Career and Leadership Development staff). Prominent recognition of partnership at the Fall and/or Spring Career & Internship Fair (based on semester(s) selected) through on-site print and digital signage. Prominent recognition of partnership on the Center for Career and Leadership Development website, within the office, on a display outside of the suite, and on the Guidebook app used for the Career & Internship Fairs. Career opportunities social media campaign on Instagram to include three graphics and two videos. Two email campaigns (once each semester) to highlight career opportunities to targeted population. Access to resume book (once during academic year) of targeted population distributed to designated employer representative. Employer registration for four representatives to annual ODU Career Summit. Custom introduction and communication to relevant student organizations (up to five). Hosted lunch and learn session with relevant student leaders and campus partners/faculty. Gold $7,500 One booth registration, admission for two representatives, and an electrical connection at the in-person Fall and Spring Career & Internship Fairs. Alternatively, the employer may choose to add an additional booth during either the Fall or Spring Career & Internship Fair in lieu of registration for two fairs. Premier booth placement at the Career & Internship Fair (based on consultation with Center for Career and Leadership Development staff). Prominent recognition of partnership at the Fall and/or Spring Career & Internship Fair (based on semester(s) selected) through on-site print and digital signage. Prominent recognition of partnership on the Center for Career and Leadership Development website, within the office, on a display outside of the suite, and on the Guidebook app used for the Career & Internship Fairs. Career opportunities social media campaign on Instagram to include three graphics and two videos. One email campaign (during year) to highlight career opportunities to targeted population. Access to resume book (once during academic year) of targeted population distributed to designated employer representative. Employer registration for three representatives to annual ODU Career Summit. Custom introduction and communication to relevant student organizations (up to three). Silver $5,000 One booth registration, admission for two representatives, and an electrical connection at the in-person Fall and Spring Career & Internship Fairs. Alternatively, the employer may choose to add an additional booth during either the Fall or Spring Career & Internship Fair in lieu of registration for two fairs. Premier booth placement at the Career & Internship Fair (based on consultation with Center for Career and Leadership Development staff). Prominent recognition of partnership at the Fall and/or Spring Career & Internship Fair (based on semester(s) selected) through on-site print and digital signage. Prominent recognition of partnership on the Center for Career and Leadership Development website, within the office, on a display outside of the suite, and on the Guidebook app used for the Career & Internship Fairs. Career opportunities social media campaign on Instagram to include two graphics and one video. One email campaign (during year) to highlight career opportunities to targeted population. Access to resume book (once during academic year) of targeted population distributed to designated employer representative. Employer registration for two representatives to annual ODU Career Summit. Bronze $2,000 One booth registration, admission for two representatives, and an electrical connection at the in-person Fall or Spring Career & Internship Fairs. Premier booth placement at the Career & Internship Fair (based on consultation with Center for Career and Leadership Development staff). Prominent recognition of partnership at the Fall and/or Spring Career & Internship Fair (based on semester(s) selected) through on-site print and digital signage. Prominent recognition of partnership on the Center for Career and Leadership Development website, within the office, on a display outside of the suite, and on the Guidebook app used for the Career & Internship Fairs. Career opportunities social media campaign on Instagram to include one graphic and one video. Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube Our Partners Thank you to our 2025-2026 Employer Partners! 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
