or GI Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Career Champions Breadcrumb Home Faculty & Staff Career Champions The Center for Career and Leadership Development is excited to announce our new Career Champions Program! Career Champions is a campus wide program designed to visibly identify faculty and staff who are especially equipped to assist students with career decision making. The Career Champion training workshops engage participants in a tailored curriculum designed to provide them with knowledge about the career development process and the foundations of employability, as well as teaching best practices for having career conversations with students.  Participants will learn valuable helping skills, goal setting techniques, ethical practices, and how best to make referrals to available resources.  Career Champions will also leave with resources they can use in their own professional career.  Those who complete the training programs will receive a Career Champions decal to display in their office, inviting students to approach them to discuss career related topics. Participants will also receive access to a Career Champions Canvas group that includes recording of all webinars, resources, and a place to ask questions and learn from colleagues. Join Career Champions today ► 8-to-Great Career Readiness Competencies ODU’s 8-to-Great Career Readiness Competencies outline the essential skills, behaviors, and knowledge Monarchs need to thrive in the workplace and confidently navigate their career journey. Learn More Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
