se schedules and needs. Learn more about STAT ► Request a LEAP STAT Student ► Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube Post a Student Opportunity (Handshake) Student Employment Hiring Action Form HR Hiring Student Employees Resources Request a STAT Student Request a VA Work Study Student Request an Allocation for a LEAP Federal Work Study VA Work Study Federal Work-Study provides part-time jobs for undergraduate and graduate students with financial need, allowing them to earn money to help pay education expenses. The encourages community service work and work related to the student's course of study. This work-study program is a VA education benefit offered to military students working towards a college degree, vocational certificate, or from ¾ to full time. In this assistance program, financial aid is traded in return for volunteering personal time. Most work-study assignments include completing and processing paperwork, assisting with recruitment services, and working at medical facilities, among other common VA duties. More information about VA Work Study ► Federal Work Study Federal Work-Study provides part-time jobs for undergraduate and graduate students with financial need, allowing them to earn money to help pay education expenses. The encourages community service work and work related to the student's course of study. VA Work Study This work-study program is a VA education benefit offered to military students working towards a college degree, vocational certificate, or from ¾ to full time. In this assistance program, financial aid is traded in return for volunteering personal time. Most work-study assignments include completing and processing paperwork, assisting with recruitment services, and working at medical facilities, among other common VA duties. More information about VA Work Study ► 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
