Cost Estimator GI Bill Benefits You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Research Division of Research Back Division of Research Research Centers Research Compliance Grants & Funding ODU Research Foundation Back ODU Research Foundation You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Life at ODU About ODU Back About ODU At a Glance Accreditation Facts & Figures History & Archives Leadership Leadership Office of the President Administration & Organization Strategic Planning & Initiatives Arts & Culture Back Arts & Culture Arts@ODU Gordon Art Galleries Diehn Concert Series Literary Festival Barry Art Museum Military & Veterans Back Military & Veterans Military Connection Center Army ROTC Navy ROTC Student Life Back Student Life Career & Leadership Development Clubs & Organizations Dining Housing & Residence Life Recreation & Wellness Service & Civic Engagement Student Engagement & Traditions You don’t have to have it all figured out. Let’s explore what inspires you - together. EXPLORE PROGRAMS Athletics Apply Visit Helpful Links Give Alumni myODU Info for Current Students Faculty & Staff Military Students Parents & Families Apply Visit Quinncia for Faculty & Staff Breadcrumb Home Faculty & Staff Quinncia For Faculty & Staff What is Quinncia? Quinncia is an AI-powered career readiness platform designed to help students strengthen their resumes, improve interviewing skills, elevator pitch, and curriculum vitae feedback, LinkedIn optimization, and prepare for internship and job opportunities. Faculty can enhance students' career readiness by integrating Quinncia into their course curriculum. Faculty may use Quinncia to assign and monitor career development activities, including resume reviews, LinkedIn profile optimization, and mock interview practice. To request faculty access, email careercoach@odu.edu with the subject line: \"Quinncia Professor Access Request.\" Once your request has been processed, you will receive a confirmation email verifying that your professor account has been activated and is ready to use. Using Quinncia Walkthrough Resources Getting Started STEP 1: Log Into Your Quinncia Account After receiving the confirmation email that your professor access has been granted, access your Quinncia account here . STEP 2: Inviting Students to Quinncia Invite students to Quinncia using one of the following two methods: Option 1: Generic Student Access Link Option 2: Upload Class Roster Faculty can upload a student roster directly into Quinncia by entering their ODU email addresses. Student Invitation Upload Guide Students are assigned directly to your designated course division rather than the default pool. This option is easier for student tracking, progress monitoring, and reporting. General Faculty Help Topics Explore management features and platform administration resources here: Further help topics Topics Include: Student management, course setup including how to break your class into separate sections, reporting features, invitation workflows. Syllabus Insert about Quinncia Services . Ways to Integrate Quinncia into Courses & Programs Incorporate Quinncia activities into your course curriculum Resume development assignments Mock interviews Internship readiness and milestone Specialized career exploration courses Follow-up with a coaching appointment Schedule an appointment on Handshake Schedule Your Career Coaching Appointment on Handshake Click on the “Career Center Tab” Click on Appointments Schedule A new appointment Need Assistance? For questions or technical assistance with Quinncia, please contact the Center for Career & Leadership Development (CCLD) at careercoach@odu.edu . We're happy to help! Using Quinncia Getting Started STEP 1: Log Into Your Quinncia Account After receiving the confirmation email that your professor access has been granted, access your Quinncia account here . STEP 2: Inviting Students to Quinncia Invite students to Quinncia using one of the following two methods: Option 1: Generic Student Access Link Option 2: Upload Class Roster Faculty can upload a student roster directly into Quinncia by entering their ODU email addresses. Student Invitation Upload Guide Students are assigned directly to your designated course division rather than the default pool. This option is easier for student tracking, progress monitoring, and reporting. Walkthrough Resources General Faculty Help Topics Explore management features and platform administration resources here: Further help topics Topics Include: Student management, course setup including how to break your class into separate sections, reporting features, invitation workflows. Syllabus Insert about Quinncia Services . Ways to Integrate Quinncia into Courses & Programs Incorporate Quinncia activities into your course curriculum Resume development assignments Mock interviews Internship readiness and milestone Specialized career exploration courses Follow-up with a coaching appointment Schedule an appointment on Handshake Schedule Your Career Coaching Appointment on Handshake Click on the “Career Center Tab” Click on Appointments Schedule A new appointment Need Assistance? For questions or technical assistance with Quinncia, please contact the Center for Career & Leadership Development (CCLD) at careercoach@odu.edu . We're happy to help! Career Development Resources Quinncia also includes on-demand resources to support continued growth. Students have access to instructional videos, downloadable guides, mock interview tools, and an extensive help library to reinforce learning and build career readiness skills independently. Quinncia Overview Quinncia Resume Development & ATS Readiness Assignment Stand Out in AI Interviews with Quinncia Center for Career & Leadership Development Home About Us Students Leadership & Professional Development Career Coaching & Job Search Service Learning Experiential Learning Student Employment Living-Learning & Theme Communities Quinncia Employers Career Fairs ODU Career Summit Employer Advisory Board Employer Partners Eligibility Guidelines Faculty & Staff Career Champions Classroom Presentations On-Campus Student Employment Letters of Reference Employer Referrals Quinncia for Faculty Alumni Events Contact Center for Career & Leadership Development 2202 Webb University Center Norfolk, VA 23529 757-683-4388 office ccld@odu.edu Directory Instagram linkedin youtube 5115 Hampton Blvd, Norfolk,          VA 23529 Contact Facebook Instagram YouTube LinkedIn Resources Employment Directories University Libraries Alumni Legal Legal & Compliance Privacy Accessibility Health & Safety Emergency Management Campus Hazing Transparency Visit Visit ODU Transportation & Parking Campus Map Copyright © Old Dominion University • Updated 2025"
